{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-tags-page-tsx","path":"/blog/tags/notes/","result":{"data":{"tags":{"group":[{"fieldValue":"EVs","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"adventofcode","totalCount":3},{"fieldValue":"ai","totalCount":3},{"fieldValue":"ansible","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"artifacts","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"binary analysis","totalCount":3},{"fieldValue":"bluesky","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"bqn","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"cars","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"decompilation","totalCount":4},{"fieldValue":"decompiler","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"dogs","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"fostering","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"fuzzing","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"ghidra","totalCount":3},{"fieldValue":"home","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"linux","totalCount":5},{"fieldValue":"llm","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"notes","totalCount":3},{"fieldValue":"notion","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"papers","totalCount":8},{"fieldValue":"personal","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"pharos","totalCount":3},{"fieldValue":"profiling","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"programming","totalCount":5},{"fieldValue":"prolog","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"publications","totalCount":6},{"fieldValue":"quick thoughts","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"rescue","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"research","totalCount":11},{"fieldValue":"reverse engineering","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"rust","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"skiing","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"talks","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"travel","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"ubuntu","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"web","totalCount":3}]},"posts":{"totalCount":3,"edges":[{"node":{"htmlAst":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Can existing neural decompiler artifacts be used to run on a "},{"type":"element","tagName":"em","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"new"}]},{"type":"text","value":" example?  Here are some notes on the current state of the art.  I assign each decompiler a score from 0 to 10 based on how easy it is to use the publicly available artifacts to run on a new example."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"slade-210","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#slade-210","ariaLabel":"slade 210 permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.12520"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"SLaDe"}]},{"type":"text","value":": 2/10"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"SLaDe has a publicly released "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://zenodo.org/records/10205121"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"replication artifact"}]},{"type":"text","value":" but there are several problems that prevent it from being used on new examples:"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"ol","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The models are trained on assembly code produced from compilers rather than disassemblers.  This is probably minor."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"More problematically, SLaDe uses IO testcases during beam search to help detect the best candidate.  It can be used without these, but the results will be worse.  SLaDe does not contain a mechanism for producing testcases for new examples."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Below is a quote from a private conversation with the author:"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"blockquote","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"You are right that IO are somehow used to select in the beam search, in the sense that we report pass@5. They are not strictly required to get the outputs though."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The link you sent is for the program synthesis dataset. In this one, IO generation was programmatic but still kind of manual, I don't think it would be feasible to automatically generate the props file in the general case. For the Github functions, we have a separate repo that automatically generates IO tests, but those are randomly generated and the quality depends on each case. If I had to redo now, I would ask an LLM to generate unit tests! I can give you access to the private repo we used to automatically generate the IO examples for the general case if you wish, but now I'd do it with LLMs rather than randomly."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"llm4decompile-910","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#llm4decompile-910","ariaLabel":"llm4decompile 910 permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/albertan017/LLM4Decompile/tree/main"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"LLM4Decompile"}]},{"type":"text","value":": 9/10"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"LLM4Decompile has published model files on HuggingFace that can easily be used\nto run on new examples.  I created a few "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/ejschwartz/llm4decompile-9b-v2"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"HuggingFace\nSpaces"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for\ntesting."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"resym-210","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#resym-210","ariaLabel":"resym 210 permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://www.cs.purdue.edu/homes/lintan/publications/resym-ccs24.pdf"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"resym"}]},{"type":"text","value":": 2/10"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"resym has a publicly released "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/lt-asset/resym"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"replication\nartifact"}]},{"type":"text","value":".  Unfortunately, as of February\n2025, the artifact is "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/lt-asset/resym/issues/2"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"missing the \"prolog-based inference system for struct\nlayout recovery\""}]},{"type":"text","value":" which is the key\ncontribution of the paper.  Thus it is not possible to run resym on new\nexamples."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"degpt-810","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#degpt-810","ariaLabel":"degpt 810 permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://www.ndss-symposium.org/wp-content/uploads/2024-401-paper.pdf"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"DeGPT"}]},{"type":"text","value":": 8/10"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"DeGPT has a publicly released "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/PeiweiHu/DeGPT"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"GitHub\nrepository"}]},{"type":"text","value":".  I'm largely going on memory,\nbut I used it previously on new examples and it was relatively easy to use.  "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/PeiweiHu/DeGPT/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20state%3Aclosed%20author%3Aedmcman"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I\ndid have to file a few PRs\nthough."}]}]}],"data":{"quirksMode":false}},"timeToRead":2,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2025-02-25--notes-neural-decompiler-artifacts/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["notes","research","decompilation"],"title":"Notes: Neural Decompiler Artifacts","updatedDate":"25 February, 2025","image":null,"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/ad998/ed.png 70w","sizes":"35px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/dbb7e/ed.webp 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/299bc/ed.webp 70w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"35px"}]},"width":35,"height":35}}}}}}},{"node":{"htmlAst":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page documents my experience with \"pressure washing\" my vinyl fence and\nsiding.  I have pressure washing in quotes, because it's SH or sodium\nhypochlorite (or bleach) that does the bulk of the work.  Pros often call this\n\"soft washing\"."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For vinyl fence soft washing, you want around 1-2% SH.  Most household bleach is\n6% SH, so if you mix 1 part bleach with 5 parts water, you'll get around 1% SH."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"You also want to use a surfectant to help the mixture stick to the fence.  I\nused Dawn Ultra.  Some people claim that some dish soaps will cause a bad\nreaction with the bleach, ranging from \"mustard gas\" to neutralizing the bleach."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I personally found that at 1-1.5% SH, the mixture was safe to use around grass.\nI wet the grass before and after applying the mixture, and I didn't see any\ndamage."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"supplies","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#supplies","ariaLabel":"supplies permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Supplies"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"ul","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://www.amazon.com/Chapin-International-20000-1-Gallon-Translucent/dp/B000E28UQU/ref=sr_1_2_sspa?dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.O_3AJHxmUqW699ofxZyHsog5sRcy5HcZQ5JY6ySS3PJbWTPPJbbftsrm5T1YP3HHUnrqawsL89DT0XKVoJ3QvSgX4v0NqcJpUtW5KMOL5hZeCSP_pv0Ghw1fX8m2WLhkIYtzPdVCVDcFa1xsoIh-yEox3HygBtB1-TKMYhM4E5-J9_NoP1uqJunwOMFZgQeeH7LJpE7YPkcO2BuxC8nyHNqzQEMmxU1A40O5A-57ilvJoibvmn4onXpXOiFCW5QaEvhdKXRol6AvejVqZMvb_L8AigquF-IOzdmNyUfbB8A.agDZ1kCD8r4RGrqYpcLs-ihgv0mY2zga1T4PGutOgPA&dib_tag=se&keywords=pump+sprayer&qid=1731869145&sr=8-2-spons&sp_csd=d2lkZ2V0TmFtZT1zcF9hdGY&psc=1"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1 Gallon Pump Sprayer"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0BK3HYR5F/ref=ppx_yo_dt_b_search_asin_title?ie=UTF8&psc=1"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Measuring cup"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://www.amazon.com/Dawn-Ultra-Dishwashing-Liquid-Original/dp/B0773QWZ7X/ref=sr_1_2_pp?dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.Igd67dB5i6JYa7j1IU09RFDZ2kHIC4hIjLeoEvOa8p8QGQ29GgYMAR-sUGVQgzCqTaxN3zbGNHeXBU1mkl8Nh-PitFF2R14h9q-E4T_zwpGqI7W2BBeinPCAoSSo_0FEZrDumu1npkqvKZRZxCNsdbQKdbkMbkgjy6vBNqmcFymCAHMX_RU93fOR6EUprcVyOcRlBXziNHMDS1Vdt_RflPd1DbsEKfvWe2cGq3Lu5U2ji79FcPT-SjvejoyjOzihkey6ZWvJoRMc_bbBVCn0dQBuP9tb0IieHDJKk5hRCdU.emD9LvR3mOT6LhgLfiPr7Im1gXDN8wAvOPKdvVdzDpM&dib_tag=se&keywords=dawn+ultra&qid=1731869232&sr=8-2"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dawn Ultra"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whatever 6% bleach you can find"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"recipe","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#recipe","ariaLabel":"recipe permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Recipe"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"ol","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add 3 cups of 6% SH bleach"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add 0.8 gallons of water"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add 2 fl. oz. of Dawn Ultra"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Make sure to put the soap in last, or your mixture will foam up and overflow the\nsprayer when you try to close it."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spray the mixture on the fence, let it sit for about five minutes, and then\nrinse it off.  You can use a garden hose, but I personally found that using a\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://www.homedepot.com/pep/RYOBI-ONE-18V-EZClean-320-PSI-0-8-GPM-Cordless-Battery-Cold-Water-Power-Cleaner-Tool-Only-RY120350/312453233?source=shoppingads&locale=en-US&pla&utm_source=google&utm_medium=vantage&utm_campaign=23679&utm_content=25332&mtc=SHOPPING-RM-RMP-GGL-D25P-Multi-NA-RYOBI_2574-NA-PMAX-NA-NA-MK862159001-23679-NBR-2574-NA-VNT-FY24Q1_Q4_RYOBI_D25P_RM__AON_OPE&cm_mmc=SHOPPING-RM-RMP-GGL-D25P-Multi-NA-RYOBI_2574-NA-PMAX-NA-NA-MK862159001-23679-NBR-2574-NA-VNT-FY24Q1_Q4_RYOBI_D25P_RM__AON_OPE-20990828848--&gad_source=1&gclid=CjwKCAiAxea5BhBeEiwAh4t5KyVICnWHwlyscntFyhbSpwdDWoYWQFqrLfiDabZtpkOoyqoUxo7SvBoCkI0QAvD_BwE&gclsrc=aw.ds"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ryobi One+\nEZ-Clean"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nworked better.  I'm sure a pressure washer would have been even faster, but it\nis less convenient to use."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"That's about it.  This removed most of the staining."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For some areas that had large amounts of growth, I used a "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://www.homedepot.com/pep/RYOBI-ONE-18V-Cordless-Telescoping-Power-Scrubber-Tool-Only-P4500/311738437?g_store=&source=shoppingads&locale=en-US&pla&utm_source=google&utm_medium=vantage&utm_campaign=23678&utm_content=25331&mtc=SHOPPING-RM-RMP-GGL-D25P-Multi-NA-RYOBI_3338-NA-PMAX-NA-NA-MK862139001-23678-NBR-3338-NA-VNT-FY24Q1_Q4_RYOBI_D25P_RM__AON_CPT&cm_mmc=SHOPPING-RM-RMP-GGL-D25P-Multi-NA-RYOBI_3338-NA-PMAX-NA-NA-MK862139001-23678-NBR-3338-NA-VNT-FY24Q1_Q4_RYOBI_D25P_RM__AON_CPT-20990829250--&gad_source=1&gclid=CjwKCAiAxea5BhBeEiwAh4t5KysO1cS0U-OwtLrmUqnV4HDVxNiZbQTlqdXrzhpcY039zazEGd7h7BoCV4oQAvD_BwE&gclsrc=aw.ds"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ryobi\nScrubber"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nto physically remove it before spraying."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","pro